Subject: [PATCH] [NEEDS_HUMAN] Hard-coded fallback bearer tokens (and accepted empty tokens) authen

Fix default-credential:notesapp/storage.py:USERS.

Root cause: storage.py derives user credentials from os.environ.get with hard-coded public defaults and never validates the result (non-empty, minimum strength, distinct per user). current_user trusts USERS without question, so a missing or empty configuration becomes a known or empty credential instead of a startup failure.

Fix strategy: Remove the hard-coded defaults. At import or startup, require each token env var to be set to a secret of at least 16 characters, and require tokens to be distinct across users. Fail closed with RuntimeError otherwise. Update the existing test to supply its own tokens through the environment.

